    "result_text": "The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation lives in `OwnerMapper.locality(Owner)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`), which populates the `locality` field on the owner DTO.\n\n**What I changed:** It now prefers the postcode. I added a `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) and a helper `regionFromPostcode(...)` that returns the matching region for a 4-digit postcode. `locality(...)` tries the postcode first and only falls back to the existing city-to-region table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else `UNKNOWN`) when the postcode is absent or in no known range. Also added the `java.util.Map` import.\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Known cities with a matching postcode return the same region as before (e.g. Sydney + 2000 \u2192 NSW).\n- A city sharing a name is now disambiguated by its postcode (e.g. an unknown/random city with postcode 3000 \u2192 VIC), matching the new `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` test.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, which is the whole suite).",
