    "probe_text": "The controller order is confirmed. Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, as handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:150`).\n\n## Before the method runs \u2014 declarative gates\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must be an owner-admin, else the method never executes.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`, fails as 400 `MethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-separated words)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(1..255)` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (optional)\n   - `postcode`, `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no bean-validation constraints\n\n## Inside `addOwner` \u2014 in exact execution order\n\nValidations (V) throw custom exceptions; side-effects (S) mutate the owner or the DB.\n\n1. **V \u2014 `validateRequiredFields`** \u2014 firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone must be non-blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n2. **V \u2014 `validatePostcode`** \u2014 if a postcode is present, must be 4 digits within the city's region range (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n3. **S \u2014 map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n4. **S \u2014 normalize address** (`normalizeAddress`): trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; stored on owner.\n5. **S \u2014 default & roll registration date**: if absent use `LocalDate.now()`; then `toBusinessDay` rolls Sat/Sun forward to Monday; stored on owner.\n6. **V \u2014 `rejectWhenDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 \u2265100 owners already on that (business) registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n7. **V \u2014 `rejectWhenCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 \u226550 owners already in that city \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n8. **S \u2014 `applyHousehold`**: find existing owners with same normalized lastName+address; if any, compute a stable `householdId` (`HH-` + first 12 hex of SHA-256 of `lastNameKey|addressKey`), set it on the new owner, **and back-fill that householdId onto each existing household member via `saveOwner(existing)`** \u2014 so this one request can write multiple owner rows.\n9. **S \u2014 normalize telephone** to E.164 (`normalizeTelephone`); invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400) (+61 requires 9 national digits, +1 requires 10). Stored.\n10. **S \u2014 normalize email** to lowercase, or null (`normalizeEmail`); if present must match the email pattern \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400). Stored.\n11. **V \u2014 `rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 full `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) matches an existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n12. **S \u2014 assign `customerCode`** (`nextCustomerCode`): `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, sequence = per-city owner count + 1.\n13. **S \u2014 assign `membershipNumber`** (`membershipNumber`): `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n14. **S \u2014 set `namesakeCount`** (`countNamesakes`): count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n15. **S \u2014 persist the new owner** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`, `em.persist`).\n16. **S \u2014 map to response** `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`, which also reads all owners and derives response-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`).\n17. **S \u2014 audit log** \u2014 the `\"AUDIT\"` SLF4J logger emits `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026`.\n18. **S \u2014 set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notable points\n\n- **No entity lifecycle hooks**: `Owner`/`Person`/`BaseEntity` have no `@PrePersist`/`@EntityListeners`. All defaulting and derivation happens in the controller. The entity's `@Pattern` E.164 constraint on `telephone` (and `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city) would only fire if the JPA provider bean-validates on persist; the controller pre-normalizes telephone to satisfy it.\n- **No password hashing, no email/notification sending, no Spring events** anywhere in this path. The only hashing (SHA-256) is for deriving `householdId`.\n- **`sharesHousehold` is dead input**: documented as controlling same-household duplicate rejection, but `addOwner`/`applyHousehold` never read `getSharesHousehold()`. Household detection always just assigns a shared `householdId`; it never rejects. That documented behavior is not implemented."
